# Implements port slice 2 (A2; the author's q37 answer, LMX_blog/2026-09-27.md: the formal is written as
# in his example, `op(fn: (int: x) int)`): a callable formal whose contract is its header written in
# place.  `apply` takes `inc` for it and calls it: 11.  The header is registered as a descriptor-only
# method `apply(op)` -- the formal's contract, as a bodiless `fn:` named in `(test3: f)` is -- and
# `inc` is admitted against it by signature.  Before, the formal was refused: "incompatible entry
# signature".  Success is 7.
fn: inc (int: x) int
    return: x + 1
end: inc

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    return: op(value)
end: apply

int: ok 7
if: apply(inc 10) != 11
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
